    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use direct substitution to show that each limit leads to the indeterminate form $${0/0}.$$ Then, evaluate the limit.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="93" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\underset{x\rightarrow 4}{\lim }\frac{x^{2} - 16}{x - 4}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$limx\to 4x2-16x-4=16-164-4=00;limx\to 4x2-16x-4=16-164-4=00;$$ then, $$limx\to 4x2-16x-4=limx\to 4(x+4)(x-4)x-4=8limx\to 4x2-16x-4=limx\to 4(x+4)(x-4)x-4=8$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
